# wave_T0 = 1792555200  (bar_ts of first live wave_log row: gateio BTC/USDT:USDT 4h bar 2026-10-21 04:00 UTC; logged_at 1792570904 = 2026-10-21 08:21:44 UTC by dashboard PID 2180, structure_version structure_v1)
# ledger: research.db trials family=structure_wave_fwd_v1 dataset=gate_structure_fwd_2026-10-21 (registered 2026-10-21, N 58->60 together with structure_chart_fwd_v1)
# 2026-10-24 I-2026-10-24-01 (data integrity; additive — frozen .md unchanged). OPERATIONAL DECISION, not pre-authorised by the frozen text:
#   frozen §4 makes a data-integrity failure a kill condition ('판정불가'), and §3-4 ('데이터 공백 … 공백 비율 보고') concerns missing bars inside
#   resolution windows — neither covers corrupt log rows. Fact: 8 of the first 11 wave_log rows had a close different from the exchange's final close
#   (truncated last candles of v1 pagination / in-progress snapshots promoted from the 1 h pickle); the 3 1d rows' frames held a fake bar too.
#   Rule (mechanical, outcome-blind): every row with logged_at < meta.loader_v2_live_ts (first start of the fixed loader, set once) is listed in
#   wave_log_quarantine and treated as NOT LOGGED — the frozen data model already allows missing rows (view-dependent logging, §6). Quarantined rows are
#   excluded from scoring and churn; wave_log itself is untouched (first-log-only). Hypothesis, constants and event definitions are unchanged;
#   wave_T0 stays 1792555200 (12-month deadline unchanged).
#   Re-basing: an id whose first record is quarantined is scored from its first non-quarantined row (new t0 and that row's inv/target/close/p_ref);
#   the report gives n_rebased and the max lag in bars (server _wave_scored exposes both). Under the RW null this is unbiased because scoring restarts
#   at the new t0 with that row's own inv/target/p_ref (Markov property); the selection rule itself ignores outcomes.
#   No 4h event could mature before ~2026-11-07, but resolutions before maturity (target/invalidation touched in the first bars) may have been visible on
#   the chart when the rule was fixed — neutrality rests only on the rule ignoring outcomes. Any residual integrity failure found at judgement still
#   means 판정불가 (frozen §4).
# P1b hourly job (logged_by 'job', in-process thread in the SYSTEM dashboard, polls every 60 s, logs each new closed bar 75 s after close):
#   live from 2026-10-24T12:00:08Z (meta.job_live_ts, read from the live structure.db on 2026-10-27; dashboard process started 2026-10-24T12:00:01Z
#   = meta.loader_v2_live_ts); meta.job_live_ts = logged_at of the first wave_log row the job actually INSERTED (set once — a job attempt on a bar a
#   view already logged does not set it). Rows are written only for the 3-symbol pool (BTC/ETH/SOL USDT perps), only after the quarantine migration
#   succeeded (otherwise the write is withheld and retried), never while structure.db is locked at the deploy-marker read (withheld, counted as a log
#   failure, retried by the next view/job poll), and only from frames that pass the quality gate (not the 1000-bar fallback, reached the present, latest
#   closed bar <= 1 bar late, no zero-volume flat among the last 3 closed bars or at a re-fetched page junction, no missing bar among the last 3, no
#   re-fetched page-junction bar absent from the response — R5-DL-L1 2026-10-27; other flats / other missing bars are warnings only).
# 2026-11-03 A 27-cell job (additive — frozen .md unchanged): wave_log rows are gateio-only by the new exchange gate in server_api._forward_log_append
#   (_WAVE_LOG_EXCHANGE = 'gateio'; applies to views and to the hourly job alike). The job now also runs binance/bybit cells (27 cells, gateio first) for
#   the display cache, the weekly RW controls and the closed-bar archive; those cells write no wave_log row and never set wave_T0 / wave_T0_meta /
#   job_live_ts (their status is read-only: wave.skipped_kind 'exchange', counted neither as a log failure nor in cells_logged). Before this change the
#   pool check alone would have let a binance view write an exchange=binance row (none ever did). Verify FAILs on COUNT(wave_log WHERE exchange != 'gateio') > 0.
# 2026-11-11 §3-3 SCORER CORRECTION, I-2026-11-10-01 (additive — frozen .md unchanged). Type: implementation defect — the frozen text states the
#   condition, the scorer omitted it. Found 2026-11-10 by the P1 case-tracker design review (frozen text read against server_api._wave_scored).
#   Decided 2026-11-11 by the owner on the engineering recommendation. No target-first / invalidation-first comparison was made for any event;
#   the rule is mechanical and follows the frozen text, so its neutrality does not rest on blindness: the live scorer has counted the one
#   affected event (below) in the panel's BTC 1h n_scored since it matured (about 2026-11-02), and the chart shows the bars after every t0.
#   Frozen §3-3 defines a valid event as 'd_inv > 0, d_tgt > 0 (현재가가 두 가격 사이)' and lists '거리 ≤ 0' among the 채점 불가 cases, while §2
#   stores d_inv and d_tgt as absolute distances; the scorer (it also feeds the §4 trigger count n_scored) checked only 'd > 0', so it admitted a
#   t0 row whose target is already behind the close (or whose invalidation price is on the wrong side). Such an event resolves almost
#   mechanically on the next bar (up: high >= target_price), and its p_ref = d_inv / (d_inv + d_tgt) is not the gambler's-ruin reference of §1,
#   which presumes a start between the two barriers.
#   Rule (mechanical; every exchange/symbol/tf): a t0 row is a valid event only if its close lies strictly between the two prices on the count's
#   side — direction 'up': inv_price < close < target_price; 'down': target_price < close < inv_price — i.e. the §3-3 distances taken with the
#   count's sign are both > 0. On every logged row this reading and the plain min < close < max reading agree. A failing row — exact equality
#   (distance 0) included — is 채점 불가 in the frozen '거리 ≤ 0' class; the server reports every such row that has a finite close and meets the
#   other §3-3 conditions as n_unscorable_not_between (inside n_unscorable). First record only (§3-2): an id whose first non-quarantined row
#   fails is never scored from a later row. The same valid-event set feeds H2 (§3-8) and the §3-9 figures. wave_log rows keep their recorded
#   p_ref (frozen §2 computes it whenever both absolute distances are > 0), so a non-null p_ref does not imply validity — this rule decides it.
#   H2 touch side (same defect class, decided together): an alternative's invalidation touch is judged by the side of alt_inv_price relative to
#   the t0 close (below: low <= alt_inv_price; above: high >= alt_inv_price); alt_inv_price == close, or an alternative without a finite
#   alt_inv_price, excludes the event from H2 (counted). The top-1 invalidation always lies behind the close by construction, so this reproduces
#   §3-4 for it. Second-ranked counts can be complete (their invalidation can then lie on the far side of the close for their own direction's
#   touch rule, which would score an automatic touch) or point the other way (the top-1 direction's touch rule would mis-score them); the side
#   rule handles both. So far, valid events whose alternative's invalidation lies on that far side: 1h 5 of 44 — all opposite-direction
#   completed zigzags whose alt_inv_price equals the top-1 inv_price, so D_i = 0 by construction (the report states this tie count) — 4h 0 of
#   11, 1d 0 of 2.
#   Unchanged: hypothesis, constants (src/structure.py and src/possibility.py untouched), windows, p_ref formula, seed, trigger thresholds,
#   wave_T0. Ledger: not a new trial (trials id 63 unchanged, N stays 60). The judgement report lists the failing events under §8 '거리 ≤ 0'
#   with counts and ids, states the statistic under the pre-fix check as a non-confirmatory secondary analysis (identical whenever no judged
#   event fails the rule), and runs only after the OpenTimestamps proof of this sidecar as of the commit adding this block is complete (a
#   manual stamp of exactly those bytes; the proof, with the byte length and sha256 it covers, is kept in the private repository under
#   docs/ots/ — the public record's nightly anchors cover the data files only, not this file). Enforced in the live server from the deploy
#   recorded below; before it, the panel's BTC 1h n_scored included the affected event.
#   Data available at the decision: single-event outcomes are visible on the chart by design (no event-level blinding — chart sidecar DECISION
#   2026-11-03); no forward hit rate, Δ̄ or CI of this family has been computed (no judgement script exists; the server exposes counts only).
#   Exposure (from each event's first non-quarantined wave_log row — entry-state columns; no OHLC frame loaded, no resolution computed; rows up
#   to bar_ts 1794366000 = 2026-11-11T03:00:00Z): 4h pool 16 events, 11 valid under the old check, 0 fail the rule; 1h 64 events, 45
#   old-valid, 1 fails — wave_log id 457, BTC/USDT:USDT 1h, bar_ts 1793235600, M:20261028T080000Z:zigzag:down:C (target 80340.7 above close
#   79978.7); 1d 5 events, 2 old-valid, 0 fail. QC, old vs new scorer on the 9 gateio cells (only the counts the API already exposes; no
#   first-touch side is output): identical everywhere except BTC 1h n_scored 11 -> 10 and n_unscorable 4 -> 5; the 4h cells have n_scored 0
#   under both (no 4h event matured yet).
